PREAMBLE

MAATAA OS is a sovereign runtime federation. This charter ("Ājñāpatra")
governs each component ("tantrāṃśa") of the work. It is a sovereign license
authored for this project rather than a stock template, but it deliberately
GRANTS THE FOUR SOFTWARE FREEDOMS in full so that the work is, in substance,
open source. This document does not claim certification by the Open Source
Initiative; it claims only that the freedoms below are granted unconditionally
except for the reciprocal and attribution terms stated.

1. GRANT OF FREEDOMS

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or sovereign
entity obtaining a copy of this work and associated files (the "Work"), to:

  (a) USE the Work for any purpose, private or public, without royalty;
  (b) STUDY how the Work operates and inspect its complete source;
  (c) MODIFY the Work and adapt it to any need; and
  (d) REDISTRIBUTE copies, original or modified, to anyone.

2. SOURCE AVAILABILITY (transparency)

Any conveyed binary or hosted/network service built from the Work must make
the complete corresponding source — including modifications — available to its
recipients or users under this same charter. Evidence and provenance files
shipped with the Work must not be stripped when redistributed.

3. SHARE-ALIKE (reciprocity)

Redistributions and derivative works must be licensed, as a whole, under this
same TANTRĀṂŚA ĀJÑĀPATRA v1.0 (or a later version published for MAATAA OS).
You may add your own notices but may not impose terms that revoke the freedoms
in Section 1 for downstream recipients.

4. ATTRIBUTION

Retain this charter, the copyright line, and existing attribution and
provenance notices in all copies and substantial portions of the Work.

5. SOVEREIGNTY & NO-FALSE-CLAIM

Nothing in this charter authorizes use of the Work to misrepresent its
verification status. Redistributors must not present unverified capabilities
as production-ready, certified, or sovereign-complete. The Work's own honest
status (CONTROLLED_NO_GO unless evidenced) must be preserved when conveyed.

6. NO WARRANTY

THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR
COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER
IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN
CONNECTION WITH THE WORK OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE WORK.

END OF CHARTER
